<div id="S5.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Effect of explicit constraints for similarity map <math id="S5.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span>
In Table <a href="#S5.T7" title="Table 7 ‣ 5.3 Ablation Study ‣ 5 Experiment ‣ UGround: Towards Unified Visual Grounding with Unrolled Transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>, Exp. 1, 2, and 5 optimize the similarity map against hard labels (binary masks), while Exp. 3, 4, and 6 optimize it against soft labels (continuous masks). The results demonstrate that converting the ground-truth mask into a Gaussian heatmap smooths the object boundaries,
leading to performance gains of +2.21% gIoU and +3.52% cIoU when comparing Exp. 5 and Exp. 6.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S5.T8" class="ltx_table ltx_align_floatright" style="width:38%;">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 8: </span>Ablation study on reward.</figcaption>
<div id="S5.T8.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:151.0pt;height:34.5pt;vertical-align:-15.5pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-32.1pt,7.3pt) scale(0.701764910428784,0.701764910428784) ;">
<table id="S5.T8.2.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="S5.T8.2.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S5.T8.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_th_row ltx_border_r ltx_border_tt" style="padding-left:8.5pt;padding-right:8.5pt;">Exp. ID</th>
<th id="S5.T8.2.1.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt" style="padding-left:8.5pt;padding-right:8.5pt;"><math id="S5.T8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{bce}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{bce}</annotation></semantics></math></th>
